{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c58f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae78-f771-79c0-aef9-997901ed5074"},"sequence":290,"recorded_at":1780531400000575,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae79-8148-7913-a25d-e2c8a41e7bd1"},"task_id":"01a0ae79-8148-7913-a25d-e2c8a41e7bd1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae79-8148-7913-a25d-e2c8a41e7bd1","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2zvo8m/TASK-260830-2zvo8m_conformance-matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2zvo8m conformance matrix — native-resume smoke framework\n2|\n3|Pinned authority: `relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0`\n4|(`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`). Each row maps one in-scope clause\n5|to its production call site and named committed test, or to a stated\n6|bound. \"Proven\" means a named test drives the production entry and\n7|fails when the behavior is weakened (see the narrowing mutants in\n8|`internal/resumesmoke/mutant_test.go`).\n9|\n10|## Section 7.5 — provider operations used by the smoke\n11|\n12|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n13||---|---|---|\n14|| probe identifies exact build; typed failures stay opaque | `Run.probe` → `Host.Call(OpProbe)` → `ProbeBuild` | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts` (pass rows), `TestSmokeProbeMismatchFails` |\n15|| identify-session with session, provider, observation; closed confidence | `Run.identify` → `Host.Call(OpIdentifySession)` → `SplitIdentifyResult` | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts`, `TestSmokeStrongConfidenceFails` |\n16|| resume over identity, workspace_paths, execution_profile, terminal, lease; SpawnPlan result | `Run.resume` → `ResolveMapping` → `Host.Call(OpResume)` → `DecodeSpawnPlan` | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts`, `TestSmokePiUnmappedVersionFails`, `TestSmokeThroughRealProviderProcess` |\n17|| Deeper request-body member semantics | Adapter-owned | Bound: params boundary validates IDs, deadline, profile, workspace absoluteness, terminal geometry, lease shape, observation bounds; the adapter refuses the rest under 7.5 |\n18|\n19|## Section 7.6 — quiescence (read-only precondition input)\n20|\n21|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n22||---|---|---|\n23|| valid safe proof consumed as precondition; unsafe stops graceful work | `Run.quiescence` → `DecodeQuiesceProof` | Proven: `TestSmokeSafeQuiescencePasses`, `TestSmokeUnsafeQuiescenceFails` |\n24|| absent proof never fails the smoke (no mutation of its own) | `Run.quiescence` skip arm | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts` (quiescence skipped on every row) |\n25|| proof-to-tuple provider/version binding | Quiescence owner | Bound: stated in `doc.go`; the smoke consumes valid-and-safe only |\n26|\n27|## Section 7.7 — execution profiles (smoke consumption)\n28|\n29|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n30||---|---|---|\n31|| stored profile maps for the probed build or resume fails `profile_mapping_unavailable` | `Run.resume` → `ResolveMapping` | Proven: `TestSmokePiUnmappedVersionFails` (detail names the failure) |\n32|\n33|## Section 7.8 — smoke as target-write precondition\n34|\n35|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n36||---|---|---|\n37|| bounded native-resume smoke evidence exists in the closed record shape | `Run` → `Record` → `VerifyRecord` | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts` (every row verifies), `TestSmokeRecordCarriesNoCapabilityClaim` |\n38|| record carries checks with pass/fail/skipped, digests, timestamps; no secrets, no raw native references | `Record` encoding + `assertNoCanary` | Proven: every row test asserts the canary-free record; `TestSmokeTamperedRecordRefuses` |\n39|| evidence pointer for the Section 13.14 registry object | `evidence_digest` integration point | Bound: the detailed record is what a registry entry points at; the registry object itself stays owned by `internal/sessadapter` (untouched) |\n40|\n41|## Section 8.2 — native-store inventory\n42|\n43|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n44||---|---|---|\n45|| discovery over the declared native roots incl. XDG default, Pi override | `Run.bind` → `StoreRootFor` | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts` (store root asserted on pass rows) |\n46|| native Windows rows bind with native separators | `StoreRootFor` + proof root rule | Bound: needs a Windows host; 4 rows skip loudly on POSIX with cells pinned by derivation |\n47|\n48|## Section 8.3 — capability matrix (no advertisement)\n49|\n50|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n51||---|---|---|\n52|| smoke advertises no capability; Section 8.3 stays the only authority | Record shape (no capability/doctor surface) | Proven: `TestSmokeRecordCarriesNoCapabilityClaim` (closed 16-member shape) |\n53|\n54|## Section 8.4 — support matrix (native-resume direction)\n55|\n56|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n57||---|---|---|\n58|| all 27 rows read their native-resume cell | `ResumeCell` | Proven: `TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow` (derived from pinned text, 27-row guard) |\n59|| matrix agrees with the landed tuple gate on every row | `ResumeCell` vs `CheckResumeTuple` | Proven: `TestResumeMatrixAgreesWithTupleGate` |\n60|| A rows pass end to end | `Run` | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts` (A subtests) |\n61|| C rows gate the resume plan; U/? refuse with zero calls | `Run` cell arms | Proven: `TestSmokeRowVerdicts` (C/U/? subtests + call assertions) |\n62|| unknown never rewritten as unsupported | `Cell` + `Verdict` vocabularies | Proven: distinct `unknown`/`unsupported` verdicts asserted per row |\n63|| WSL2 and native Windows never collapse | `platformCell` distinct rows | Proven: separate subtests per row in derivation and verdict suites |\n64|\n65|## Appendix B — version gates\n66|\n67|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n68||---|---|---|\n69|| Muse macOS arm64 accepts only the probed 0.1.0; newer behavior unsettled | `museCell` pin + `?` off-pin | Proven: `TestResumeMatrixCoversEverySpecRow` (pin + off-pin), `TestSmokeMuseOnePatchOffPinRefuses` |\n70|| Antigravity resume only when the backend realm resolves | `Run.bind` → `VerifyIdentityDiscovery` realm rule | Proven: `TestSmokeAntigravityUnresolvedRealmFails`, gated Antigravity rows with resolved realm |\n71|\n72|## Section 19.3 — promotion rule\n73|\n74|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n75||---|---|---|\n76|| smoke never promotes a gated cell; promotion needs published evidence | no promotion path in `Run`; `VerifyRecord` consistency | Proven: `TestSmokePromotionAttemptRefuses` (flipped + resigned), `TestSmokeInconsistentFailRefuses`; C detail cites Section 19.3 |\n77|\n78|## Durability and crash behavior (evidence record mutates durable state)\n79|\n80|| Clause | Call site | Evidence |\n81||---|---|---|\n82|| no-replace + fsync install; identical retry reuses; disagreement quarantines | `Store` | Proven: `TestStoreInstallsVerifiedRecord`, `TestStoreReplayIsIdentical`, `TestStoreDisagreementQuarantines` |\n83|| crash hooks recover | `StoreHooks` | Proven: `TestStoreCrashBeforeCreateAdmitsNothing`, `TestStoreCrashAfterWriteReplays` |\n84|| real kill between write and fsync recovers byte-identical evidence | `Store` via re-executed helper | Proven: `TestStoreRealKillBetweenWriteAndSync` |\n85|| identical inputs replay byte-identical records | `Run` determinism | Proven: `TestSmokeIdenticalInputsReplayIdenticalBytes` |","final_result":true}}}
