{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c849","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae78-f771-79c0-aef9-997901ed5074"},"sequence":639,"recorded_at":1780531400001273,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae7a-6315-78d1-8ef4-a66982fc2df0"},"task_id":"01a0ae7a-6315-78d1-8ef4-a66982fc2df0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae7a-6315-78d1-8ef4-a66982fc2df0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/resumesmoke/smoke.go`.\n1|package resumesmoke\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"fmt\"\n7|\t\"sort\"\n8|\t\"strings\"\n9|\t\"time\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// This file runs one bounded native-resume smoke: a provider-specific\n16|// probe, identify-session, discovery-bind, quiescence-precondition,\n17|// and resume-plan sequence against one adapter executable through\n18|// provhost.Host.Call, recorded as one closed smoke record.\n19|//\n20|// The check order is the refusal order. The Section 8.4 cell decides\n21|// before any adapter call: unsupported and unknown tuples are\n22|// refused with no call at all, so a refused tuple can neither mutate\n23|// nor observe provider state. Available and conditional tuples pass\n24|// the tuple gate, then the exact-version probe, then identification\n25|// at exact confidence, then the discovery binding over the declared\n26|// native root and backend realm, then the optional quiescence\n27|// precondition, and only an available cell reaches the resume plan —\n28|// a conditional cell gates it with the Section 19.3 promotion\n29|// citation. Any failure stops the run at its check: later checks\n30|// are absent from the record, never invented.\n31|//\n32|// Every adapter response is validated by the landed Section 7\n33|// decoders and replayed through the validated members, never the\n34|// raw body. The record digests the validated bytes; check details\n35|// carry digests, member names, and gate citations only, never\n36|// native references or secrets.\n37|\n38|// smokeTimeFormat stamps record timestamps in the scalar timestamp\n39|// shape: UTC RFC3339 with milliseconds.\n40|const smokeTimeFormat = \"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00\"\n41|\n42|// Check names in execution order.\n43|const (\n44|\tcheckCell       = \"resume-cell\"\n45|\tcheckGate       = \"tuple-gate\"\n46|\tcheckProbe      = \"probe\"\n47|\tcheckIdentify   = \"identify\"\n48|\tcheckBind       = \"discover-bind\"\n49|\tcheckQuiescence = \"quiescence\"\n50|\tcheckResume     = \"resume-plan\"\n51|)\n52|\n53|// Terminal carries the Section 7.5 TerminalDescriptor fixture one\n54|// smoke run resumes with.\n55|type Terminal struct {\n56|\tBackend     string\n57|\tTerminalID  string\n58|\tInteractive bool\n59|\tColumns     int\n60|\tRows        int\n61|}\n62|\n63|// Lease carries the Section 7.5 LeaseToken fixture: the session,\n64|// the epoch above zero, and the UUIDv4 lease ID.\n65|type Lease struct {\n66|\tSessionID string\n67|\tEpoch     uint64\n68|\tLeaseID   string\n69|}\n70|\n71|// Observation carries the Section 7.5 ProcessObservation fixture.\n72|// Candidate lists are sorted unique, as the contract requires.\n73|type Observation struct {\n74|\tTerminalID          string\n75|\tExecutablePath      string\n76|\tStartedAt           string\n77|\tCandidateStorePaths []string\n78|\tCandidateNativeIDs  []string\n79|}\n80|\n81|// Params carries everything one smoke run needs: the claimed tuple,\n82|// the host and adapter executable to drive, the request envelope\n83|// facts, the session, workspace, terminal, lease, and observation\n84|// fixtures, the discovery and quiescence precondition inputs, and\n85|// the clock. Timestamps in the record come from Clock, so identical\n86|// params with a fixed clock replay byte-identical records.\n87|type Params struct {\n88|\tTuple       provhost.BuildTuple\n89|\tHost        provhost.Host\n90|\tExecutable  string\n91|\tDeadline    string\n92|\tProbeID     string\n93|\tIdentifyID  string\n94|\tResumeID    string\n95|\tSessionID   string\n96|\tRealm       string\n97|\tWorkspaces  map[string]string\n98|\tProfile     string\n99|\tTerminal    Terminal\n100|\tLease       Lease\n101|\tObservation Observation\n102|\tHome        string\n103|\tXDGDataHome string\n104|\tStoreRoot   string\n105|\tDiscovery   []byte\n106|\tQuiescence  []byte\n107|\tClock       func() time.Time\n108|}\n109|\n110|// Report is one finished smoke run: the decoded record and its\n111|// canonical bytes, ready to store.\n112|type Report struct {\n113|\tRecord Record\n114|\tBytes  []byte\n115|}\n116|\n117|// Run executes one smoke run and returns its report. Params errors\n118|// and internal encoding failures return a Go error with no report;\n119|// every specified refusal is a verdict in the report, never an\n120|// error, because a refusal is the run's honest outcome.\n121|func Run(ctx context.Context, params Params) (*Report, error) {\n122|\tclock := params.Clock\n123|\tif clock == nil {\n124|\t\tclock = time.Now\n125|\t}\n126|\tdeadline, err := checkParams(params, clock)\n127|\tif err != nil {\n128|\t\treturn nil, err\n129|\t}\n130|\tstarted := clock().UTC().Format(smokeTimeFormat)\n131|\tcell, gate := ResumeCell(params.Tuple.ProviderID, params.Tuple.ProviderVersion, params.Tuple.Platform, params.Tuple.Architecture)\n132|\trun := &runner{\n133|\t\tctx:      ctx,\n134|\t\tparams:   params,\n135|\t\tdeadline: deadline,\n136|\t\tcell:     cell,\n137|\t\tgate:     gate,\n138|\t\tstarted:  started,\n139|\t\trecord: Record{\n140|\t\t\tSchema:        RecordSchema,\n141|\t\t\tSchemaVersion: RecordSchemaVersion,\n142|\t\t\tTuple: Tuple{\n143|\t\t\t\tProviderID:      params.Tuple.ProviderID,\n144|\t\t\t\tProviderVersion: params.Tuple.ProviderVersion,\n145|\t\t\t\tPlatform:        params.Tuple.Platform,\n146|\t\t\t\tArchitecture:    params.Tuple.Architecture,\n147|\t\t\t},\n148|\t\t\tResumeCell: cell,\n149|\t\t\tGateRef:    gate,\n150|\t\t\tStartedAt:  started,\n151|\t\t},\n152|\t}\n153|\trun.note(checkCell, OutcomePass, cellDetail(cell, gate))\n154|\tif cell == CellUnsupported || cell == CellUnknown {\n155|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n156|\t}\n157|\tif err := provhost.CheckResumeTuple(params.Tuple); err != nil {\n158|\t\trun.note(checkGate, OutcomeFail, \"tuple gate refused the claimed build\")\n159|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n160|\t}\n161|\trun.note(checkGate, OutcomePass, \"tuple gate admitted the claimed build\")\n162|\tif _, _, ok := run.probe(); !ok {\n163|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n164|\t}\n165|\tidentity, ok := run.identify()\n166|\tif !ok {\n167|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n168|\t}\n169|\tif ok := run.bind(identity.Identity); !ok {\n170|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n171|\t}\n172|\tif ok := run.quiescence(); !ok {\n173|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n174|\t}\n175|\tif ok := run.resume(identity.Identity); !ok {\n176|\t\treturn run.finish(clock)\n177|\t}\n178|\treturn run.finish(clock)\n179|}\n180|\n181|// runner carries one run's accumulating record.\n182|type runner struct {\n183|\tctx      context.Context\n184|\tparams   Params\n185|\tdeadline scalar.Timestamp\n186|\tcell     Cell\n187|\tgate     string\n188|\tstarted  string\n189|\trecord   Record\n190|}\n191|\n192|// note appends one check to the record.\n193|func (run *runner) note(name string, outcome Outcome, detail string) {\n194|\trun.record.Checks = append(run.record.Checks, Check{Name: name, Outcome: outcome, Detail: detail})\n195|}\n196|\n197|// finish stamps completion, derives the verdict, encodes, and\n198|// self-verifies the record before returning it.\n199|func (run *runner) finish(clock func() time.Time) (*Report, error) {\n200|\trun.record.CompletedAt = clock().UTC().Format(smokeTimeFormat)\n201|\trun.record.Verdict = deriveVerdict(run.cell, run.record.Checks)\n202|\tencoded, err := encodeRecord(run.record)\n203|\tif err != nil {\n204|\t\treturn nil, err\n205|\t}\n206|\tdecoded, err := VerifyRecord(encoded)\n207|\tif err != nil {\n208|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke run encoded an invalid record: %w\", err)\n209|\t}\n210|\treturn &Report{Record: decoded, Bytes: encoded}, nil\n211|}\n212|\n213|// probe calls the probe operation, replays the exact probed build,\n214|// and fails closed on any drift from the claimed tuple.\n215|func (run *runner) probe() (provhost.BuildTuple, string, bool) {\n216|\tbody, err := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\n217|\t\t\"platform\":               run.params.Tuple.Platform,\n218|\t\t\"architecture\":           run.params.Tuple.Architecture,\n219|\t\t\"provider_executable\":    nil,\n220|\t\t\"requested_capabilities\": []string{\"native_resume\"},\n221|\t})\n222|\tif err != nil {\n223|\t\trun.note(checkProbe, OutcomeFail, \"probe request is unframeable\")\n224|\t\treturn provhost.BuildTuple{}, \"\", false\n225|\t}\n226|\tresponse, err := run.call(provhost.OpProbe, run.params.ProbeID, body)\n227|\tif err != nil {\n228|\t\trun.note(checkProbe, OutcomeFail, \"probe call failed: \"+shortError(err))\n229|\t\treturn provhost.BuildTuple{}, \"\", false\n230|\t}\n231|\tprobed, err := provhost.ProbeBuild(response.Body)\n232|\tif err != nil {\n233|\t\trun.note(checkProbe, OutcomeFail, \"probe response is not a valid probe: \"+shortError(err))\n234|\t\treturn provhost.BuildTuple{}, \"\", false\n235|\t}\n236|\tif probed != run.params.Tuple {\n237|\t\trun.note(checkProbe, OutcomeFail, \"probe build drifted from the claimed tuple\")\n238|\t\treturn provhost.BuildTuple{}, \"\", false\n239|\t}\n240|\tdigest := digestBytes(response.Body)\n241|\trun.record.ProbeDigest = digest\n242|\trun.note(checkProbe, OutcomePass, \"exact-version probe matches the claimed tuple\")\n243|\treturn probed, digest, true\n244|}\n245|\n246|// identify calls identify-session and requires exact confidence:\n247|// the smoke binds one precise native identity, never a guess.\n248|func (run *runner) identify() (provhost.IdentifyOutcome, bool) {\n249|\tvar empty provhost.IdentifyOutcome\n250|\tobservation := map[string]any{\n251|\t\t\"terminal_id\":           run.params.Observation.TerminalID,\n252|\t\t\"executable_path\":       run.params.Observation.ExecutablePath,\n253|\t\t\"started_at\":            run.params.Observation.StartedAt,\n254|\t\t\"candidate_store_paths\": run.params.Observation.CandidateStorePaths,\n255|\t\t\"candidate_native_ids\":  run.params.Observation.CandidateNativeIDs,\n256|\t}\n257|\tbody, err := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\n258|\t\t\"session_id\":  run.params.SessionID,\n259|\t\t\"provider_id\": run.params.Tuple.ProviderID,\n260|\t\t\"observation\": observation,\n261|\t})\n262|\tif err != nil {\n263|\t\trun.note(checkIdentify, OutcomeFail, \"identify request is unframeable\")\n264|\t\treturn empty, false\n265|\t}\n266|\tresponse, err := run.call(provhost.OpIdentifySession, run.params.IdentifyID, body)\n267|\tif err != nil {\n268|\t\trun.note(checkIdentify, OutcomeFail, \"identify call failed: \"+shortError(err))\n269|\t\treturn empty, false\n270|\t}\n271|\toutcome, err := provhost.SplitIdentifyResult(response.Body, run.params.Tuple.ProviderID)\n272|\tif err != nil {\n273|\t\trun.note(checkIdentify, OutcomeFail, \"identify response is not a valid result: \"+shortError(err))\n274|\t\treturn empty, false\n275|\t}\n276|\tif outcome.Confidence != \"exact\" {\n277|\t\trun.note(checkIdentify, OutcomeFail, \"identify confidence is below exact\")\n278|\t\treturn empty, false\n279|\t}\n280|\tidentityID, err := pluckRecordID(outcome.Identity)\n281|\tif err != nil {\n282|\t\trun.note(checkIdentify, OutcomeFail, \"identify record carries no digest identity\")\n283|\t\treturn empty, false\n284|\t}\n285|\trun.record.IdentityRecordID = identityID\n286|\trun.note(checkIdentify, OutcomePass, \"session identified at exact confidence\")\n287|\treturn outcome, true\n288|}\n289|\n290|// bind resolves the Section 8.2 declared native root and binds the\n291|// observed discovery proof to the identified record: the exact\n292|// native ID, the discovery fact, the root containment, and the\n293|// backend realm the tuple requires. A proof for another tuple\n294|// refuses here.\n295|func (run *runner) bind(identity []byte) bool {\n296|\troot, backendOnly, err := provhost.StoreRootFor(run.params.Tuple.ProviderID, run.params.Home, run.params.XDGDataHome)\n297|\tif err != nil {\n298|\t\trun.note(checkBind, OutcomeFail, \"store root is not declared for this provider: \"+shortError(err))\n299|\t\treturn false\n300|\t}\n301|\tdiscovery := provhost.DiscoveryContext{\n302|\t\tBuild:             run.params.Tuple,\n303|\t\tHome:              run.params.Home,\n304|\t\tXDGDataHome:       run.params.XDGDataHome,\n305|\t\tRealm:             run.params.Realm,\n306|\t\tStoreRootOverride: run.params.StoreRoot,\n307|\t}\n308|\tif err := provhost.VerifyIdentityDiscovery(identity, run.params.Discovery, discovery); err != nil {\n309|\t\trun.note(checkBind, OutcomeFail, \"discovery proof does not bind to the identity: \"+shortError(err))\n310|\t\treturn false\n311|\t}\n312|\tif !backendOnly {\n313|\t\trun.record.StoreRoot = root\n314|\t}\n315|\trun.record.DiscoveryProofDigest = digestBytes(run.params.Discovery)\n316|\trun.note(checkBind, OutcomePass, \"discovery proof binds the identity to its store\")\n317|\treturn true\n318|}\n319|\n320|// quiescence consumes the optional Section 7.6 precondition input:\n321|// a supplied proof must be valid and safe, because graceful work\n322|// stops on an unsafe boundary. An absent proof skips the check —\n323|// the smoke performs no mutation of its own — and never fails it.\n324|func (run *runner) quiescence() bool {\n325|\tif run.params.Quiescence == nil {\n326|\t\trun.note(checkQuiescence, OutcomeSkipped, \"no quiescence proof input; smoke performs no mutation\")\n327|\t\treturn true\n328|\t}\n329|\tsafe, err := provhost.DecodeQuiesceProof(run.params.Quiescence)\n330|\tif err != nil {\n331|\t\trun.note(checkQuiescence, OutcomeFail, \"quiescence proof is not a valid proof: \"+shortError(err))\n332|\t\treturn false\n333|\t}\n334|\tif !safe {\n335|\t\trun.note(checkQuiescence, OutcomeFail, \"quiescence proof is unsafe; graceful work stops\")\n336|\t\treturn false\n337|\t}\n338|\trun.record.QuiescenceDigest = digestBytes(run.params.Quiescence)\n339|\trun.note(checkQuiescence, OutcomePass, \"quiescence precondition is safe\")\n340|\treturn true\n341|}\n342|\n343|// resume plans the native resume: the stored profile must map for\n344|// the probed build, and the adapter must return a valid spawn plan.\n345|// Only an available cell reaches the adapter here; any other cell\n346|// gates the plan with the Section 19.3 promotion citation, and that\n347|// gate can never be promoted by the smoke itself.\n348|func (run *runner) resume(identity []byte) bool {\n349|\tif run.cell != CellAvailable {\n350|\t\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomeSkipped, \"resume plan gated on \"+run.gate+\"; promotion only by section 19.3\")\n351|\t\treturn true\n352|\t}\n353|\tif _, err := provhost.ResolveMapping(run.params.Tuple.ProviderID, run.params.Profile, run.params.Tuple); err != nil {\n354|\t\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomeFail, \"stored profile has no mapping for the probed build: \"+shortError(err))\n355|\t\treturn false\n356|\t}\n357|\tbody, err := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\n358|\t\t\"identity\":          json.RawMessage(identity),\n359|\t\t\"workspace_paths\":   run.params.Workspaces,\n360|\t\t\"execution_profile\": run.params.Profile,\n361|\t\t\"terminal\": map[string]any{\n362|\t\t\t\"backend\":     run.params.Terminal.Backend,\n363|\t\t\t\"terminal_id\": run.params.Terminal.TerminalID,\n364|\t\t\t\"interactive\": run.params.Terminal.Interactive,\n365|\t\t\t\"columns\":     run.params.Terminal.Columns,\n366|\t\t\t\"rows\":        run.params.Terminal.Rows,\n367|\t\t},\n368|\t\t\"lease\": map[string]any{\n369|\t\t\t\"session_id\":  run.params.Lease.SessionID,\n370|\t\t\t\"lease_epoch\": run.params.Lease.Epoch,\n371|\t\t\t\"lease_id\":    run.params.Lease.LeaseID,\n372|\t\t},\n373|\t})\n374|\tif err != nil {\n375|\t\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomeFail, \"resume request is unframeable\")\n376|\t\treturn false\n377|\t}\n378|\tresponse, err := run.call(provhost.OpResume, run.params.ResumeID, body)\n379|\tif err != nil {\n380|\t\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomeFail, \"resume call failed: \"+shortError(err))\n381|\t\treturn false\n382|\t}\n383|\tplatform, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(run.params.Tuple.Platform)\n384|\tif err != nil {\n385|\t\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomeFail, \"tuple platform is not a registry member\")\n386|\t\treturn false\n387|\t}\n388|\tif err := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(response.Body, run.params.Tuple.ProviderID, run.params.Profile, platform); err != nil {\n389|\t\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomeFail, \"resume plan is not a valid spawn plan: \"+shortError(err))\n390|\t\treturn false\n391|\t}\n392|\trun.record.SpawnPlanDigest = digestBytes(response.Body)\n393|\trun.note(checkResume, OutcomePass, \"adapter returned a valid resume plan\")\n394|\treturn true\n395|}\n396|\n397|// call frames one request and drives it through the provider host.\n398|func (run *runner) call(operation provhost.Operation, requestID string, body []byte) (provhost.Response, error) {\n399|\tparsed, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(requestID)\n400|\tif err != nil {\n401|\t\treturn provhost.Response{}, err\n402|\t}\n403|\treturn run.params.Host.Call(run.ctx, run.params.Executable, provhost.Request{\n404|\t\tOperation: operation,\n405|\t\tRequestID: parsed,\n406|\t\tDeadline:  run.deadline,\n407|\t\tBody:      body,\n408|\t})\n409|}\n410|\n411|// cellDetail renders the resume-cell check detail for one cell.\n412|func cellDetail(cell Cell, gate string) string {\n413|\tswitch cell {\n414|\tcase CellAvailable:\n415|\t\treturn \"section 8.4 available cell \" + gate + \"; runtime probe still decides\"\n416|\tcase CellConditional:\n417|\t\treturn \"section 8.4 conditional cell \" + gate + \"; resume plan gated, promotion only by section 19.3\"\n418|\tcase CellUnsupported:\n419|\t\treturn \"section 8.4 unsupported cell \" + gate + \"; refused with no adapter call\"\n420|\tdefault:\n421|\t\treturn \"section 8.4 unknown cell \" + gate + \"; refused with no adapter call\"\n422|\t}\n423|}\n424|\n425|// shortError renders one failure for a check detail: the message\n426|// text only, truncated, with no values the error may carry.\n427|func shortError(err error) string {\n428|\tmessage := err.Error()\n429|\tif index := strings.IndexByte(message, '\\n'); index >= 0 {\n430|\t\tmessage = message[:index]\n431|\t}\n432|\tif len(message) > 200 {\n433|\t\tmessage = message[:200]\n434|\t}\n435|\treturn message\n436|}\n437|\n438|// pluckRecordID reads the record_id digest from validated identity\n439|// bytes. The caller established the bytes as a valid Provider\n440|// Identity Record; the digest shape is rechecked here so a drifted\n441|// pluck fails closed instead of recording garbage.\n442|func pluckRecordID(identity []byte) (string, error) {\n443|\tvar members map[string]json.RawMessage\n444|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(identity, &members); err != nil {\n445|\t\treturn \"\", err\n446|\t}\n447|\tvar recordID string\n448|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(members[\"record_id\"], &recordID); err != nil {\n449|\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"identity record_id is not a string\")\n450|\t}\n451|\tif !isDigest(recordID) {\n452|\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"identity record_id is not a digest\")\n453|\t}\n454|\treturn recordID, nil\n455|}\n456|\n457|// checkParams validates the run params: the adapter address, the\n458|// request envelope facts, the profile vocabulary, the Section 7.5\n459|// fixture ranges the smoke depends on, and the required discovery\n460|// precondition input. It returns the parsed deadline.\n461|func checkParams(params Params, clock func() time.Time) (scalar.Timestamp, error) {\n462|\tvar zero scalar.Timestamp\n463|\tif params.Executable == \"\" {\n464|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke executable is empty\")\n465|\t}\n466|\tdeadline, err := scalar.ParseTimestamp(params.Deadline)\n467|\tif err != nil {\n468|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke deadline is not a timestamp: %w\", err)\n469|\t}\n470|\tinstant, err := deadline.Time()\n471|\tif err != nil {\n472|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke deadline is not an instant: %w\", err)\n473|\t}\n474|\tif !clock().Before(instant) {\n475|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke deadline is not in the future\")\n476|\t}\n477|\tfor _, member := range []struct {\n478|\t\tname  string\n479|\t\tvalue string\n480|\t}{\n481|\t\t{\"probe request id\", params.ProbeID},\n482|\t\t{\"identify request id\", params.IdentifyID},\n483|\t\t{\"resume request id\", params.ResumeID},\n484|\t\t{\"session id\", params.SessionID},\n485|\t} {\n486|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(member.value); err != nil {\n487|\t\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke %s is not a UUIDv7: %w\", member.name, err)\n488|\t\t}\n489|\t}\n490|\tif params.Profile != \"standard\" && params.Profile != \"yolo\" {\n491|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke profile is not standard or yolo\")\n492|\t}\n493|\tif len(params.Discovery) == 0 {\n494|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke discovery proof input is absent\")\n495|\t}\n496|\tplatform, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(params.Tuple.Platform)\n497|\tif err != nil {\n498|\t\treturn zero, fmt.Errorf(\"smoke tuple platform is not a registry member: %w\", err)\n499|\t}\n500|\tif err := checkParamsFixtures(params, platform); err != nil {\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c84b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae78-f771-79c0-aef9-997901ed5074"},"sequence":640,"recorded_at":1780531400001275,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae7a-6315-78d1-8ef4-a66982fc2df0"},"task_id":"01a0ae7a-6315-78d1-8ef4-a66982fc2df0","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae7a-6315-78d1-8ef4-a66982fc2df0"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c84d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae78-f771-79c0-aef9-997901ed5074"},"sequence":641,"recorded_at":1780531400001277,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae7a-64b2-7593-bb05-23c764e91dd3"},"task_id":"01a0ae7a-64b2-7593-bb05-23c764e91dd3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae7a-64b2-7593-bb05-23c764e91dd3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/resumesmoke/doc.go`.\n1|// Package resumesmoke runs the host-side bounded native-resume smoke\n2|// the pinned specification names as a target-write precondition\n3|// (Section 7.8): a provider-specific discover, read, identify, and\n4|// resume-plan sequence against one provider adapter, with any\n5|// unsupported tuple claim refused.\n6|//\n7|// The smoke drives the landed provider host: every adapter call goes\n8|// through provhost.Host.Call, and every response is validated by the\n9|// landed Section 7 decoders — probe (7.4), identify-session (5.5),\n10|// discovery binding over the Section 8.2 declared native roots, and\n11|// the resume SpawnPlan (7.5). Quiescence (7.6) and the discovery\n12|// proof enter as read-only precondition inputs the smoke validates\n13|// and binds but never produces: proving quiescence and observing\n14|// discovery belong to their owners, not to this framework.\n15|//\n16|// Each run records a closed Native Resume Smoke record\n17|// (urn:ax:schema:native-resume-smoke 1.0.0): the claimed tuple, the\n18|// Section 8.4 native-resume cell, the verdict, digests of the probe,\n19|// discovery proof, identity record, and spawn plan, the store root,\n20|// every check with its pass, fail, or skipped outcome, and\n21|// timestamps. The record carries no secrets and no raw native\n22|// references — only digests, the documented store root, and check\n23|// facts. It is the detailed evidence a Section 13.14\n24|// ResumeSmokeEvidence registry entry points at through its\n25|// evidence_digest; the registry object itself stays owned by\n26|// internal/sessadapter.\n27|//\n28|// Refusal is the point, not an edge. A tuple whose Section 8.4\n29|// native-resume cell is conditional, unsupported, or unknown, or\n30|// that Appendix B leaves unsettled, can never pass: unsupported and\n31|// unknown tuples are refused before any adapter call, conditional\n32|// tuples gather read-only probe, identify, and binding evidence and\n33|// then gate the resume plan, and no smoke API promotes a gated or\n34|// refused cell — promotion belongs to Section 19.3 evidence the\n35|// smoke never produces. A passing smoke never advertises a\n36|// capability: the Section 8.3 capability matrix stays the only\n37|// capability authority, so this package carries no capability map\n38|// and no doctor surface.\n39|//\n40|// Stated bounds: request-body member ranges (terminal geometry,\n41|// lease shape, workspace absoluteness) are validated for the tuple\n42|// platform at the params boundary, but deeper adapter-body semantics\n43|// stay the adapter's to refuse under Section 7.5; the quiescence\n44|// precondition is consumed as valid-and-safe only, and binding the\n45|// proof's own provider and version to the tuple belongs to the\n46|// quiescence owner. Record integrity detects tampering and naive\n47|// promotion, not a forgery that recomputes both the digest and a\n48|// consistent check list: smoke records are local evidence with no\n49|// adversary, and the no-promotion property is that no production\n50|// path emits pass for a non-available cell.\n51|package resumesmoke","final_result":true}}}
