{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d1c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae78-f771-79c0-aef9-997901ed5074"},"sequence":1852,"recorded_at":1780531400003699,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d66f8436-fc6e-4b44-8a69-1ce280f51ff5"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae81a61a75039e895c76db8cff01","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-60-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-2zvo8m) { checklist }' 2>&1 | head -c 4000; echo; echo \\\"=====TRY2=====\\\"; task-board m --help 2>&1 | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Query task checklist projection\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Run provider-specific discover/read/resume/identity checks and refuse unsupported tuple claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tests green\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\\"done\\\":false}]}\\n\\n=====TRY2=====\\nExecute a write operation against the board using the DSL.\\n\\nMutations:\\n  set_status(ID, status=..., commit_ack=scope_committed?)\\n                                        Change status; acknowledge enforced done transitions\\n  normalize_legacy_status(ID, expected_raw=..., status=...)\\n                                        Repair one exact unparseable raw status (local boards)\\n  handoff(ID, role=..., status=...)     Verify checklist/outcome evidence and change status\\n  set_estimate(ID, estimate=..., ...)  Set Task/Bug story-point estimate\\n  create(type=..., name=..., ...)      Create element\\n  set_details(ID, title=..., ...)      Update README fields\\n  rename(ID, name=...)                 Rename element name/slug\\n  delete(ID)                           Delete element (destructive)\\n  assign(ID, agent=...)                Assign agent\\n  unassign(ID)                         Remove assignment\\n  link(ID, blocked_by=...)             Add dependency\\n  unlink(ID, blocked_by=...)           Remove dependency\\n  check_item(ID, item=N)              Check checklist item\\n  uncheck_item(ID, item=N)            Uncheck checklist item\\n  add_checklist_item(ID, text=...)     Add checklist item\\n  remove_checklist_item(ID, item=N)    Remove obsolete checklist item (destructive)\\n  set_notes(ID, text=..., set=bool?)   Append/set notes\\n  set_parent(ID, parent=...)           Move to new parent\\n  accept_cr(ID, revision=N, evidence=...) Record a reviewer acceptance of a Change Request revision (local board only)\\n  integrate_external(ID, evidence=...)     Close accepted empty-delta external work by evidence (local board only)\\n  withdraw_cr(ID, revision=N, reason=...) Retire an unintegrated revision (local board only)\\n  defer_cr(ID, revision=N, reason=...)    Mark an accepted revision deferred by human decision (local board only)\\n  undefer_cr(ID, revision=N)              Clear the deferral marker (local board only)\\n  add_resource(ID, name=..., content=..., type=..., description=...)\\n  update_resource(ID, name=..., content=..., type=..., description=...)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4947,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1237,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
